+**This repository rules `JavaScript`, a departure from the recommendation.**
+Why neither recommended language fits:
+
+- Express has been published to npm as a JavaScript package since 2010, and
+  `index.js`, `lib/`, `test/` and `examples/` are all CommonJS JavaScript.
+  There is no `.ts` or `.py` file and no `tsconfig.json`.
+- It runs on Node.js (`"engines": { "node": ">= 18" }`) with no build step:
+  `package.json` `files` ships `index.js` and `lib/` exactly as written.
+  TypeScript would add a compile step to every release and change the
+  artefact published to npm.
+- Its own dependencies (`router`, `body-parser`, `send`, `serve-static`…)
+  are JavaScript packages of the same ecosystem.
+- Types for consumers are maintained outside this repository, in
+  `@types/express`.
 
-The Alternatives Considered below were weighed by governance without
